<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    kuna issue testcase: an ARM load or store through a register that holds a
    datum's address files a reference in the cross-reference index.

    Issue:      kuna-analysis-armderef - `kuna xrefs` asked for the references to an ARM global
                answered only the instruction that loaded its address from a
                GOT slot or a literal-pool word, never the `ldr`/`str
                [rN,#off]` that read and wrote it through that register.
    Stage:      P1 code/data partition - the on-demand cross-reference query
                (`listing/xrefs.rs`, `listing/kuna_picpool.rs`).

    The Listing tier and the xref query are built only on the real-object
    bootstrap path, never on the console decompile path (docs/spec/
    01-program-prep.md section 1.6), and no console command prints an xref
    row, so a stage test cannot assert the row itself. This case pins that
    the rule is inert in the rendered C of `abs_write`, whose two stores
    through a pool-loaded `g_cfg` across calls are the instruction shape it
    concerns. The row-level proof (a Read or Write of each address accessed)
    lives in the cargo gate `decompiler/crates/kuna-console/tests/verify_armderef.rs`,
    over the `armderef_arm_le32` fixture this case also loads.

    The XML wrapper only supplies the harness architecture; the pass clears it
    and loads the real linked ARM fixture (built from
    decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/armderef_arm_le32.c).
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/armderef_arm_le32</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load function abs_write</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="KUNA-ARMDEREF #1: abs_write's second call, between its two stores through g_cfg, renders" min="1" max="1">^  sink\(1\);$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="KUNA-ARMDEREF #2: abs_write renders its first call" min="1" max="1">^  sink\(0\);$</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
